  "_doc": "08 §3.2 — the four SS sets' 2/4/6-piece bonuses, as effect DSL data. A set is identified by its family axis: there is exactly one set per axis, drops.json authors a null setId because no setId vocabulary exists, and the axis is what an SS item's family already resolves to — so a second identifier here would be a second answer. The piece counts are drops.json#/sets/breakpoints and are cross-checked against it rather than restated as a rule. Effects are embedded rather than referenced: an effect is never a file. ⚠️ A null effects array is an unauthorised bonus, not an absent one — 08 §3.2 describes all twelve in prose and six of them name a mechanism that does not exist or a magnitude nobody wrote, and inventing either is the hole the null exists to keep visible. Ironvow's six-piece is authored against 16 D49's valueMode NEGATE and carries NO value on purpose — the voided hit has no HP number, which is what let it be authored without inventing one (M4-16g).",
